  "id": "COMPOUND:19085 - PROTEIN:5811",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between SureCN26387 and VMRC-LCP through a series of target interactions. The drug SureCN26387 is implicated in targeting Hepatocyte, which in turn is a target of Cocosamide B or 5-Oxobrucine, both of which target VMRC-LCP. This indicates that SureCN26387 may exert its effects via a downstream pathway that involves Hepatocyte and its targets. The evidence is consistent across multiple paths, with varying scores, but all converge on the same target hierarchy. The mechanism appears to involve a series of molecular interactions, where SureCN26387 may act as a modulator or activator of a pathway that ultimately leads to VMRC-LCP being targeted. The integration of these paths supports the notion that SureCN26387 is part of a broader network of interactions that influence VMRC-LCP, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
